\{\
    \cf3 "L1_MACRO_CATEGORIES_IT"\cf2 : \cf4 "Analizza le seguenti fonti. Identifica da 3 a 6 argomenti o macro-categorie fondamentali (Nodi di Livello 1) per descrivere il tema \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{rootNodeLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{optionalL1Labels\}\}\cf5 \\n\cf4 Restituisci SOLO ED ESCLUSIVAMENTE un Array JSON di stringhe. Nessun commento o testo aggiuntivo.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 FONTI:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{textParts\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "L1_MACRO_CATEGORIES_EN"\cf2 : \cf4 "Analyze the following sources. Identify 3 to 6 fundamental topics or macro-categories (Level 1 Nodes) to describe the theme \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{rootNodeLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{optionalL1Labels\}\}\cf5 \\n\cf4 Return ONLY AND EXCLUSIVELY a JSON Array of strings. No commentary or additional text.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 SOURCES:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{textParts\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "MIND_MAP_BRANCH_IT"\cf2 : \cf4 "Sei un tutor esperto. Costruisci un ramo di una Mappa Mentale JSON sull'argomento: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{rootNodeLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\cf4 ATTENZIONE: DEVI POPOLARE SOLO ED ESCLUSIVAMENTE IL SOTTO-RAMO DELLA CATEGORIA: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4  (usa il suo ID esatto come Source genitore: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 ).\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{userProfileInjection\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 REGOLE TASSATIVE:\cf5 \\n\cf4 1. INCLUDI nei 'nodes' il nodo padre esatto (\cf5 \\"\cf4 id\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 label\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 level\cf5 \\"\cf4 : 1). COME 'content' INSERISCI UN CHIARO E UTILISSIMO RIASSUNTO descrittivo della macro-area (almeno 30 parole, massimo 50 parole) per aiutare lo studente.\cf5 \\n\cf4 2. Usa TASSATIVAMENTE e rigorosamente SEMPRE L'ITALIANO per tutto l'albero. Questo vale anche per le parole di connessione logica ('rel' nei links), usa verbi italiani come \cf5 \\"\cf4 include\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 porta a\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 causa\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 \'e8 formato da\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 dipende da\cf5 \\"\\n\cf4 3. Crea nodi di Livello 2 (usa 'level': 2) per i concetti chiave derivanti da \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 . Collega ognuno al genitore inserendo in links \cf5 \\"\cf4 source\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\cf4 4. Crea nodi di Livello 3 (usa 'level': 3) figli dei nodi L2.\cf5 \\n\cf4 5. Crea nodi di Livello 4 e 5 (usa 'level': 4, 5) per approfondire ulteriormente i dettagli pi\'f9 specifici, assicurando una gerarchia profonda e completa.\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{optionalMaxBranches\}\}7. 'content' DEVE ESSERE una frase molto concisa (massimo 10 parole). 'desc' DEVE ESSERE un paragrafo descrittivo (circa 50-80 parole) che spieghi il concetto in modo chiaro in base alle fonti.\cf5 \\n\cf4 8. Identifica almeno 1 'source' specifico per ogni argomento (es. libro, autore, documento).\cf5 \\n\cf4 9. ID nodi: Usa stringhe univoche in maiuscolo (es. \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}_CONCEPT_1\cf5 \\"\cf4 ).\cf5 \\n\cf4 10. 'chunks': Inserisci un array di stringhe contenente LE ESATTE CITAZIONI ESTRATTE DALLE FONTI (copia/incolla una o pi\'f9 frasi reali dal testo per comprovare il concetto). Assicurati di includere nelle citazioni il titolo originale del documento se presente.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 FONTI DA ANALIZZARE:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{textParts\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "MIND_MAP_BRANCH_EN"\cf2 : \cf4 "You are an expert tutor. Build a branch of a JSON Mind Map on the topic: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{rootNodeLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\cf4 ATTENTION: YOU MUST POPULATE ONLY AND EXCLUSIVELY THE SUB-BRANCH OF THE CATEGORY: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4  (use its exact ID as the parent Source: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 ).\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{userProfileInjection\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 STRICT RULES:\cf5 \\n\cf4 1. INCLUDE in the 'nodes' the exact parent node (\cf5 \\"\cf4 id\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 label\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 level\cf5 \\"\cf4 : 1). AS 'content' INSERT A CLEAR AND EXTREMELY USEFUL descriptive summary of the macro-area (at least 30 words, maximum 50 words) to help the student.\cf5 \\n\cf4 2. STRICTLY and rigorously ALWAYS use ENGLISH for the entire tree. This also applies to logical connection words ('rel' in links), use English verbs like \cf5 \\"\cf4 includes\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 leads to\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 causes\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 is composed of\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 depends on\cf5 \\"\\n\cf4 3. Create Level 2 nodes (use 'level': 2) for key concepts deriving from \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 . Connect each one to the parent by inserting in links \cf5 \\"\cf4 source\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\cf4 4. Create Level 3 nodes (use 'level': 3) children of L2 nodes.\cf5 \\n\cf4 5. Create Level 4 and 5 nodes (use 'level': 4, 5) to further explore more specific details, ensuring a deep and complete hierarchy.\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{optionalMaxBranches\}\}7. 'content' MUST BE a very concise sentence (maximum 10 words). 'desc' MUST BE a descriptive paragraph (about 50-80 words) that explains the concept clearly based on the sources.\cf5 \\n\cf4 8. Identify at least 1 specific 'source' for each topic (e.g., book, author, document).\cf5 \\n\cf4 9. Node IDs: Use unique uppercase strings (e.g., \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}_CONCEPT_1\cf5 \\"\cf4 ).\cf5 \\n\cf4 10. 'chunks': Insert an array of strings containing THE EXACT QUOTATIONS EXTRACTED FROM THE SOURCES (copy/paste one or more real sentences from the text to prove the concept). Ensure that original document titles are included in the quotes if present.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 SOURCES TO ANALYZE:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{textParts\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "MIND_MAP_BRANCH_INFOMANIAK_IT"\cf2 : \cf4 "Sei un tutor. Costruisci UN PICCOLO RAMO di Mappa Mentale JSON sull'argomento: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{rootNodeLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\cf4 POPOLA SOLO LA CATEGORIA: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4  (ID genitore: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 ).\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{userProfileInjection\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 REGOLE SEMPLIFICATE:\cf5 \\n\cf4 1. INCLUDI IL NODO PADRE ESATTO (\cf5 \\"\cf4 id\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 level\cf5 \\"\cf4 : 1). In 'content' e 'desc' fai un riassunto di 30-40 parole.\cf5 \\n\cf4 2. Crea MASSIMO 5-8 NODI TOTALI (usa level 2 e 3). Non creare troppi nodi.\cf5 \\n\cf4 3. 'content' frase cortissima (5 parole). 'desc' spiegazione chiara (30-40 parole).\cf5 \\n\cf4 4. ID Nodi: stringhe semplici come \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}_1\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}_2\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\cf4 5. 'chunks': Copia 1 sola frase dal testo.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 FONTI:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{textParts\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "MIND_MAP_BRANCH_INFOMANIAK_EN"\cf2 : \cf4 "You are a tutor. Build A SMALL BRANCH of a JSON Mind Map on the topic: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{rootNodeLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\cf4 ONLY POPULATE CATEGORY: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4  (parent ID: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 ).\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{userProfileInjection\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 SIMPLIFIED RULES:\cf5 \\n\cf4 1. INCLUDE THE EXACT PARENT NODE (\cf5 \\"\cf4 id\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 level\cf5 \\"\cf4 : 1). In 'content' and 'desc' write a 30-40 word summary.\cf5 \\n\cf4 2. Create MAXIMUM 5-8 TOTAL NODES (use level 2 and 3). Do not create too many nodes.\cf5 \\n\cf4 3. 'content' very short sentence (5 words). 'desc' clear explanation (30-40 words).\cf5 \\n\cf4 4. Node IDs: simple strings like \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}_1\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}_2\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\cf4 5. 'chunks': Copy exactly 1 sentence from the text.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 SOURCES:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{textParts\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_SINGLE_IT"\cf2 : \cf4 "Sei un esperto estensore di Knowledge Graph.\cf5 \\n\cf4 Tema: \{\{rootNodeLabel\}\}.\cf5 \\n\cf4 Modalit\'e0: Knowledge Graph Relazionale Libero.\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{userProfileInjection\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 REGOLE FONDAMENTALI (Pena fallimento critico):\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Estrai concetti chiave, date, o eventi storici ('id' MAIUSCOLO univoco).\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Estrai un MASSIMO ASSOLUTO DI 15-20 NODI PRINCIPALI per garantire la sintesi. NON SUPERARE QUESTO NUMERO.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Ogni nodo ('nodes') DEVE avere: 'label' (Testo Breve), 'desc' (Paragrafo ESTREMAMENTE CONCISO di massimo 30-40 parole), e 'level' (1 per Super-Hub, 2 per Hub medi, 3 per Nodi foglia).\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Crea una FITTA RETE di RELAZIONI ('links') logiche e storicamente/tecnicamente fondate tra i nodi.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Il 'rel' nei links DEVE ESSERE esplicativo (massimo 5 parole).\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 \{\{optionalKeywords\}\}\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Usa archi relazionali tra i nodi (source, target, rel).\cf5 \\n\cf4 - 'content' \'e8 una breve frase (max 10 parole). 'desc' DEVE ESSERE un paragrafo molto conciso (max 30-40 parole).\cf5 \\n\cf4 - 'chunks' DEVE contenere un array con AL MASSIMO 1 o 2 brevissime citazioni testuali estratte dalle fonti.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 FONTI DA ANALIZZARE:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{textParts\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_SINGLE_EN"\cf2 : \cf4 "You are an expert Knowledge Graph builder.\cf5 \\n\cf4 Theme: \{\{rootNodeLabel\}\}.\cf5 \\n\cf4 Mode: Free Relational Knowledge Graph.\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{userProfileInjection\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 FUNDAMENTAL RULES (Failure is critical):\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Extract key concepts, dates, or historical events (unique UPPERCASE 'id').\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Extract an ABSOLUTE MAXIMUM OF 15-20 MAIN NODES to ensure synthesis. DO NOT EXCEED THIS NUMBER.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Each node ('nodes') MUST have: 'label' (Short Text), 'desc' (EXTREMELY CONCISE paragraph of max 30-40 words), and 'level' (1 for Super-Hubs, 2 for Medium Hubs, 3 for Leaf Nodes).\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Create a DENSE NETWORK of logical and historically/technically founded RELATIONSHIPS ('links') between nodes.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - The 'rel' in links MUST BE explanatory (max 5 words).\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 \{\{optionalKeywords\}\}\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Use relational edges between nodes (source, target, rel).\cf5 \\n\cf4 - 'content' is a short sentence (max 10 words). 'desc' MUST BE a very concise paragraph (max 30-40 words).\cf5 \\n\cf4 - 'chunks' MUST contain an array with AT MOST 1 or 2 very short textual quotes extracted from the sources.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 SOURCES TO ANALYZE:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{textParts\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "SEMANTIC_CORRELATION_IT"\cf2 : \cf4 "Sei un esperto di analisi di Knowledge Graph. Ti do due liste di concetti provenienti da due Knowledge Graph diversi. Cerca possibili correlazioni semantiche tra concetti della LISTA A e concetti della LISTA B.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 LISTA A (mappa esistente):\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{existingLabels\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 LISTA B (mappa importata):\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{newLabels\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 Rispondi SOLO con un JSON array. Ogni elemento deve avere: \cf5 \\"\cf4 source\cf5 \\"\cf4  (ID dalla lista A), \cf5 \\"\cf4 target\cf5 \\"\cf4  (ID dalla lista B), \cf5 \\"\cf4 rel\cf5 \\"\cf4  (parola di relazione in italiano, 1-3 parole).\cf5 \\n\cf4 Suggerisci TUTTE le correlazioni semanticamente significative e plausibili che trovi. Se non trovi correlazioni valide, rispondi con [].\cf5 \\n\cf4 Formato: [\{\cf5 \\"\cf4 source\cf5 \\"\cf4 :\cf5 \\"\cf4 id_a\cf5 \\"\cf4 ,\cf5 \\"\cf4 target\cf5 \\"\cf4 :\cf5 \\"\cf4 id_b\cf5 \\"\cf4 ,\cf5 \\"\cf4 rel\cf5 \\"\cf4 :\cf5 \\"\cf4 correlazione\cf5 \\"\cf4 \}]"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "SEMANTIC_CORRELATION_EN"\cf2 : \cf4 "You are a Knowledge Graph analysis expert. I will provide two lists of concepts from two different Knowledge Graphs. Search for possible semantic correlations between concepts from LIST A and concepts from LIST B.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 LIST A (existing map):\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{existingLabels\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 LIST B (imported map):\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{newLabels\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 Respond ONLY with a JSON array. Each element must have: \cf5 \\"\cf4 source\cf5 \\"\cf4  (ID from list A), \cf5 \\"\cf4 target\cf5 \\"\cf4  (ID from list B), \cf5 \\"\cf4 rel\cf5 \\"\cf4  (relationship word in English, 1-3 words).\cf5 \\n\cf4 Suggest ALL semantically significant and plausible correlations you find. If you find no valid correlations, respond with [].\cf5 \\n\cf4 Format: [\{\cf5 \\"\cf4 source\cf5 \\"\cf4 :\cf5 \\"\cf4 id_a\cf5 \\"\cf4 ,\cf5 \\"\cf4 target\cf5 \\"\cf4 :\cf5 \\"\cf4 id_b\cf5 \\"\cf4 ,\cf5 \\"\cf4 rel\cf5 \\"\cf4 :\cf5 \\"\cf4 correlation\cf5 \\"\cf4 \}]"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "SINGLE_QUIZ_TUTOR_IT"\cf2 : \cf4 "Crea una singola domanda a risposta multipla basata su questo concetto: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{nodeLabel\}\}: \{\{nodeDesc\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 . Fornisci 4 opzioni di cui solo 1 corretta."\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "SINGLE_QUIZ_TUTOR_EN"\cf2 : \cf4 "Create a single multiple-choice question based on this concept: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{nodeLabel\}\}: \{\{nodeDesc\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 . Provide 4 options, of which only 1 is correct."\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "SOCRATIC_TUTOR_IT"\cf2 : \cf4 "Agisci come un Tutor Socratico. Rispondi in italiano usando formattazione HTML (<strong>,<p>,<ul>). REGOLA FONDAMENTALE: Sii ESTREMAMENTE conciso e colloquiale. Fai al massimo UNA domanda alla volta. NON dare risposte lunghe e non elencare tutto il contesto in una volta sola. SCORE FEEDBACK (allo studente non mostrare MAI il punteggio di accuratezza): - se lo score di accuracy \'e8 uguale o inferiore al 59.99% allora rinforzalo accogliendo il suo impegno e poi fornendo un esempio di che cosa avrebbe potuto rispondere per per raggiungere un accuracy di almeno il 60.00%; - score da 60% a 85.00% non dire mai lo score e suggerisci complementi informativi che avrebbero migliorato l'accuracy del 10-15%; - score da 85.01% a 95% non dire mai lo score, complimentati per lo score e incoraggia a scegliere uno dei metodi di studio per migliorare (le informazioni sono sufficientemente immagazzinate ma bisogna migliorare la fluency e l'active recall); - score da 95.01% a 100% fai solo un complimento allo studente e incoraggialo ora ad aiutare un suo compagno a studiare (incentivazione del metodo Feynman). \{\{userProfileProfile\}\} Il tuo obiettivo primario \'e8 mantenere lo studente in uno stato di FLOW (sfida ottimale). Se l'utente manifesta difficolt\'e0, stress o fatica nel rispondere, riduci drasticamente la difficolt\'e0, evita nuove domande, offri esempi chiarificatori e rendi la conversazione pi\'f9 leggera e rassicurante. \{\{phaseInstruction\}\} \{\{kgInstruction\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "SOCRATIC_TUTOR_EN"\cf2 : \cf4 "Act as a Socratic Tutor. Respond in English using HTML formatting (, , ). CORE RULE: Be EXTREMELY concise and conversational. Ask a maximum of ONE question at a time. Do NOT provide long answers and do not dump the entire context at once. SCORE FEEDBACK (NEVER show the accuracy score to the student): - if the accuracy score is 59.99% or lower, reinforce them by acknowledging their effort and then providing an example of what they could have answered to reach at least 60.00% accuracy; - for accuracy scores from 60.00% to 85.00%, never disclose the score and suggest informative additions that would have improved accuracy by 10-15%; - for accuracy scores from 85.01% to 95%, never disclose the score, praise them for the performance, and encourage them to choose a study method to improve (the information is sufficiently retained but fluency and active recall need work); -for accuracy scores from 95.01% to 100%, simply praise the student and encourage them to help a peer study (leveraging the Feynman Technique). \{\{userProfileProfile\}\} Your primary goal is to keep the student in a state of FLOW (optimal challenge). If the user shows signs of difficulty, stress, or fatigue, drastically reduce the difficulty level, stop asking new questions, offer clarifying examples, and make the conversation lighter and more reassuring. \{\{phaseInstruction\}\} \{\{kgInstruction\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "SOTA_SECOND_BRAIN_IT"\cf2 : \cf4 "Sei un costruttore di Knowledge Graph di alto livello (SOTA Second Brain). \cf5 \\n\cf4 Il nodo genitore selezionato per l'espansione \'e8:\cf5 \\n\cf4 ID: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{targetId\}\}\cf5 \\"\\n\cf4 Label: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{targetLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\\n\\n\cf4  Nella mappa esistono gi\'e0 questi concetti (EVITA DI CREARE NUOVI NODI PER QUESTI):\cf5 \\n\cf4 [\{\{existingLabels\}\}]\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 L'utente ti ha fornito questo materiale per espandere il ramo selezionato:\cf5 \\n\\"\\"\\"\\n\cf4 \{\{sourceContent\}\}\cf5 \\n\\"\\"\\"\\n\\n\cf4 Compito:\cf5 \\n\cf4 1. Leggi il materiale ed estrai concetti che siano FIGLI o SOTTO-TEMI di \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{targetLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\cf4 2. Sii specifico e analitico. Estrai dai 5 ai 15 nuovi concetti se il testo lo permette.\cf5 \\n\cf4 3. Restituisci SOLO un JSON valido con questa struttura:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\cf5 \\n\cf4   \cf5 \\"\cf4 nodes\cf5 \\"\cf4 : [\cf5 \\n\cf4     \{\cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 id\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 RAND_ID\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 label\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 Nome Concetto\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 desc\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 Descrizione approfondita e didattica (3-4 frasi)\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 level\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \{\{targetLevel\}\},\cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 group\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \{\{targetGroup\}\}\cf5 \\n\cf4     \}\cf5 \\n\cf4   ],\cf5 \\n\cf4   \cf5 \\"\cf4 links\cf5 \\"\cf4 : [\cf5 \\n\cf4     \{\cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 source\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{targetId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 target\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 RAND_ID\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 rel\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 relazione specifica (es: causa, composto da, esempio di, conseguenza)\cf5 \\"\\n\cf4     \}\cf5 \\n\cf4   ]\cf5 \\n\cf4 \}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 REGOLE MANDATORIE:\cf5 \\n\cf4 - NON includere il nodo genitore \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{targetId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4  nella lista \cf5 \\"\cf4 nodes\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Tutti i nuovi nodi devono essere collegati tramite \cf5 \\"\cf4 links\cf5 \\"\cf4  al genitore o ad altri nuovi nodi.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Se un concetto nel testo \'e8 gi\'e0 presente nella lista dei concetti esistenti, NON crearlo come nuovo nodo, ma puoi creare un link verso di esso.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Restituisci SOLO il JSON puro."\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "SOTA_SECOND_BRAIN_EN"\cf2 : \cf4 "You are a high-level Knowledge Graph builder (SOTA Second Brain).\cf5 \\n\cf4 The parent node selected for expansion is:\cf5 \\n\cf4 ID: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{targetId\}\}\cf5 \\"\\n\cf4 Label: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{targetLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\\n\\n\cf4 These concepts already exist in the map (AVOID CREATING NEW NODES FOR THESE):\cf5 \\n\cf4 [\{\{existingLabels\}\}]\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 The user provided this material to expand the selected branch:\cf5 \\n\\"\\"\\"\\n\cf4 \{\{sourceContent\}\}\cf5 \\n\\"\\"\\"\\n\\n\cf4 Task:\cf5 \\n\cf4 1. Read the material and extract concepts that are CHILDREN or SUB-TOPICS of \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{targetLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\cf4 2. Be specific and analytical. Extract 5 to 15 new concepts if the text allows.\cf5 \\n\cf4 3. Return ONLY a valid JSON with this structure:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\cf5 \\n\cf4   \cf5 \\"\cf4 nodes\cf5 \\"\cf4 : [\cf5 \\n\cf4     \{\cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 id\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 RAND_ID\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 label\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 Concept Name\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 desc\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 In-depth educational description (3-4 sentences)\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 level\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \{\{targetLevel\}\},\cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 group\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \{\{targetGroup\}\}\cf5 \\n\cf4     \}\cf5 \\n\cf4   ],\cf5 \\n\cf4   \cf5 \\"\cf4 links\cf5 \\"\cf4 : [\cf5 \\n\cf4     \{\cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 source\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{targetId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 target\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 RAND_ID\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\n\cf4       \cf5 \\"\cf4 rel\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 specific relationship (e.g., causes, consists of, example of, consequence)\cf5 \\"\\n\cf4     \}\cf5 \\n\cf4   ]\cf5 \\n\cf4 \}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 REGOLE MANDATORIE:\cf5 \\n\cf4 - DO NOT include the parent node \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{targetId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4  in the \cf5 \\"\cf4 nodes\cf5 \\"\cf4  list.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - All new nodes must be connected via \cf5 \\"\cf4 links\cf5 \\"\cf4  to the parent or other new nodes.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - If a concept in the text is already in the list of existing concepts, DO NOT create it as a new node, but you can create a link to it.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - Return ONLY pure JSON."\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "SOTA_SECOND_BRAIN_STUDENT_IT"\cf2 : \cf4 "Sei un Tutor Pedagogico esperto. Espandi questa mappa concettuale per uno studente di scuola media.\cf5 \\n\cf4 Il nodo genitore \'e8: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{targetLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 REGOLE TASSATIVE:\cf5 \\n\cf4 1. TITOLI: Massimo 3 parole chiave per ogni nuovo nodo. Usa termini semplici.\cf5 \\n\cf4 2. LINGUAGGIO: Spiegazioni chiare, esempi pratici e frasi brevi (max 30-40 parole per nodo).\cf5 \\n\cf4 3. RELAZIONI: Usa parole di legame semplici (es: \cf5 \\"\cf4 causa\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 tipo di\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 parte di\cf5 \\"\cf4 ).\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 Restituisci solo il JSON con nodes e links.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 FONTE DA ANALIZZARE:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{sourceContent\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "SOTA_SECOND_BRAIN_STUDENT_EN"\cf2 : \cf4 "You are an expert Pedagogical Tutor. Expand this concept map for a middle school student.\cf5 \\n\cf4 The parent node is: \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{targetLabel\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 .\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 STRICT RULES:\cf5 \\n\cf4 1. TITLES: Maximum 3 keywords for each new node. Use simple terms.\cf5 \\n\cf4 2. LANGUAGE: Clear explanations, practical examples, and short sentences (max 30-40 words per node).\cf5 \\n\cf4 3. RELATIONSHIPS: Use simple linking words (e.g., \cf5 \\"\cf4 causes\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 type of\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 part of\cf5 \\"\cf4 ).\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 Return only the JSON with nodes and links.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 SOURCE TO ANALYZE:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{sourceContent\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "MIND_MAP_BRANCH_STUDENT_IT"\cf2 : \cf4 "Sei un Tutor Pedagogico esperto in didattica per la scuola media. Costruisci un ramo di una Mappa Mentale JSON per uno studente.\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{userProfileInjection\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 REGOLE TASSATIVE PER STUDENTI:\cf5 \\n\cf4 1. TITOLI DEI NODI ('label'): Devono essere brevissimi, MASSIMO 3 PAROLE CHIAVE. Usa termini semplici.\cf5 \\n\cf4 2. LINGUAGGIO: Adatta il contenuto all'et\'e0 dello studente. Usa frasi brevi, evita termini astratti complessi senza spiegarli.\cf5 \\n\cf4 3. STRUTTURA: Crea una gerarchia chiara da L1 a L5. Collega i nodi con verbi italiani semplici (es. \cf5 \\"\cf4 \'e8\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 fa parte di\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 serve per\cf5 \\"\cf4 ).\cf5 \\n\cf4 4. CONTENUTO: 'content' deve essere una sintesi di max 10 parole. 'desc' deve essere una spiegazione chiara e coinvolgente (50-70 parole).\cf5 \\n\cf4 5. ESEMPI: Inserisci esempi pratici tratti dalle fonti nella 'desc'.\cf5 \\n\cf4 6. CITAZIONI: In 'chunks', inserisci le frasi pi\'f9 significative delle fonti che aiutano a capire il concetto.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 FONTI:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{textParts\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "MIND_MAP_BRANCH_STUDENT_EN"\cf2 : \cf4 "You are an expert Pedagogical Tutor in middle school teaching. Build a branch of a JSON Mind Map for a student.\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{userProfileInjection\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 STRICT RULES FOR STUDENTS:\cf5 \\n\cf4 1. NODE TITLES ('label'): Must be very short, MAXIMUM 3 KEYWORDS. Use simple terms.\cf5 \\n\cf4 2. LANGUAGE: Adapt the content to the student's age. Use short sentences, avoid complex abstract terms without explaining them.\cf5 \\n\cf4 3. STRUCTURE: Create a clear hierarchy from L1 to L5. Connect nodes with simple English verbs (e.g., \cf5 \\"\cf4 is\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 is part of\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 is used for\cf5 \\"\cf4 ).\cf5 \\n\cf4 4. CONTENT: 'content' must be a summary of max 10 words. 'desc' must be a clear and engaging explanation (50-70 words).\cf5 \\n\cf4 5. EXAMPLES: Insert practical examples from the sources in the 'desc'.\cf5 \\n\cf4 6. QUOTES: In 'chunks', insert the most significant sentences from the sources that help understand the concept.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 SOURCES:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{textParts\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "MIND_MAP_BRANCH_STUDENT_INFOMANIAK_IT"\cf2 : \cf4 "Sei un Tutor per le scuole medie. Costruisci UN PICCOLO RAMO di Mappa Mentale JSON.\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{userProfileInjection\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 REGOLE FACILI:\cf5 \\n\cf4 1. INCLUDI IL NODO PADRE (\cf5 \\"\cf4 id\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 level\cf5 \\"\cf4 : 1). Fai un riassunto semplice di 30-40 parole.\cf5 \\n\cf4 2. Crea MASSIMO 4-6 NODI TOTALI (usa level 2 e 3). Usa parole semplici.\cf5 \\n\cf4 3. TITOLI ('label'): MASSIMO 3 PAROLE CHIAVE.\cf5 \\n\cf4 4. 'content' 5 parole max. 'desc' spiegazione per un ragazzino (30 parole max).\cf5 \\n\cf4 5. ID Nodi: semplici \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}_A\cf5 \\"\cf4 , ecc.\cf5 \\n\cf4 6. 'chunks': Copia 1 sola frase dal testo.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 FONTI:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{textParts\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "MIND_MAP_BRANCH_STUDENT_INFOMANIAK_EN"\cf2 : \cf4 "You are a middle school Tutor. Build A SMALL BRANCH of a JSON Mind Map.\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{userProfileInjection\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 EASY RULES:\cf5 \\n\cf4 1. INCLUDE THE PARENT NODE (\cf5 \\"\cf4 id\cf5 \\"\cf4 : \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}\cf5 \\"\cf4 , \cf5 \\"\cf4 level\cf5 \\"\cf4 : 1). Make a simple 30-40 word summary.\cf5 \\n\cf4 2. Create MAXIMUM 4-6 TOTAL NODES (use level 2 and 3). Use simple words.\cf5 \\n\cf4 3. TITLES ('label'): MAXIMUM 3 KEYWORDS.\cf5 \\n\cf4 4. 'content' 5 words max. 'desc' explanation for a kid (30 words max).\cf5 \\n\cf4 5. Node IDs: simple \cf5 \\"\cf4 \{\{l1NodeId\}\}_A\cf5 \\"\cf4 , etc.\cf5 \\n\cf4 6. 'chunks': Copy exactly 1 sentence from the text.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 SOURCES:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{textParts\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_SINGLE_STUDENT_IT"\cf2 : \cf4 "Sei un esperto di mappe concettuali semplificate per l'apprendimento scolastico.\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{userProfileInjection\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 OBIETTIVO: Trasforma le fonti in un Knowledge Graph visivo facile da studiare.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 REGOLE D'ORO:\cf5 \\n\cf4 - TITOLI ('label'): MASSIMO 3 PAROLE per ogni nodo. Sii estremamente sintetico.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - QUANTIT\'c0: Estrai MASSIMO 15 concetti fondamentali. Meglio pochi ma chiari.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - DESCRIZIONI ('desc'): Spiega ogni concetto come se lo stessi spiegando a un compagno di classe (max 30-40 parole).\cf5 \\n\cf4 - RELAZIONI ('links'): Crea collegamenti logici evidenti usando parole di legame semplici.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - LIVELLI: Usa level 1 per l'argomento centrale, 2 per i temi principali, 3 per i dettagli.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 \{\{optionalKeywords\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 FONTI:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{textParts\}\}"\cf2 ,\
    \cf3 "KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_SINGLE_STUDENT_EN"\cf2 : \cf4 "You are an expert in simplified concept maps for school learning.\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{userProfileInjection\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 GOAL: Transform the sources into a visual Knowledge Graph that is easy to study.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 GOLDEN RULES:\cf5 \\n\cf4 - TITLES ('label'): MAXIMUM 3 WORDS per node. Be extremely concise.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - QUANTITY: Extract a MAXIMUM of 15 fundamental concepts. Fewer but clearer is better.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - DESCRIPTIONS ('desc'): Explain each concept as if you were explaining it to a classmate (max 30-40 words).\cf5 \\n\cf4 - RELATIONSHIPS ('links'): Create obvious logical connections using simple linking words.\cf5 \\n\cf4 - LEVELS: Use level 1 for the central topic, 2 for main themes, 3 for details.\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 \{\{optionalKeywords\}\}\cf5 \\n\\n\cf4 SOURCES:\cf5 \\n\cf4 \{\{textParts\}\}"\cf2 ,\
